# Autonomous Loop (Agent Requested) — lightweight port of OmO's ulw-loop

An MVP is usually "research → structure → first version" pushed in one go. This loop finishes it without stopping midway.

## Principles
- **Don't stop before self-verification.** One cycle = plan → build → `/sip` (self quality-check) → fix gaps.
- **Accumulate learning, not code** (paperthin `re0-loop`). Let a wrong build die; carry only the lessons kept in the ontology.
- **Keep context alive with the `context-loop` skill** so the ontology doesn't rot even in autonomous runs.

## Loop
```
repeat:
  1) Decide next move → /next (Combo II: /nba → /modelchk)
  2) Pick model → apply model-routing budget guard (frontier escalation-only; degrade to Cursor-native when low)
  3) Implement (Build role) → /sip self-check
  4) After each big stage → /context-clean (Combo I: clean the ontology)
  5) On re-entry / lost context → /catchup first
stop when: goal met && /sip passes && ontology (.cursor/context/ontology.md) current.
```

## Boundaries (don't hand judgment to the loop)
- Topic selection, direction, value judgments: not handled autonomously (`harness-core` Decide layer). Present evidence to the human.
- High-risk logic (auth/payment/security): don't push autonomously; review via the Plan role on frontier first.
